{
  "schema": "adhy.course/1",
  "id": "python-decorators",
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Python Decorators: From @ Syntax to Descriptors",
  "summary": "Understand what @ really does, then write your own: decorators that keep a function's name, decorators with arguments, class decorators, and how @property works underneath. You run real Python as you go.",
  "archetype": "concept",
  "scope_class": "chapter",
  "goal": {
    "text": "Python decorators",
    "target": "curious",
    "level": "some",
    "depth": "working"
  },
  "budget": {
    "daily_min": 60,
    "days": [
      "mon",
      "tue",
      "thu",
      "sat"
    ],
    "review_min": 15,
    "test_share": 0.4,
    "weekly_slot": "sat"
  },
  "outcomes": [
    {
      "id": "o1",
      "text": "Desugar any decorated definition, stacked or with arguments, into plain calls",
      "observable": "Rewrite a given @-decorated function or class as explicit assignments and predict its printed output and call order"
    },
    {
      "id": "o2",
      "text": "Write a correct function decorator with functools.wraps that preserves metadata and handles any signature",
      "observable": "Implement a timing or logging decorator that passes *args/**kwargs through and keeps __name__ and __doc__"
    },
    {
      "id": "o3",
      "text": "Write a decorator factory that takes arguments, including the optional-argument form",
      "observable": "Implement @retry(times=3) and a decorator usable both as @dec and @dec(...)"
    },
    {
      "id": "o4",
      "text": "Apply common decorator patterns: registration, caching, attribute tagging and class decorators",
      "observable": "Build a plugin registry decorator and a class decorator that adds a method, and explain when each runs"
    },
    {
      "id": "o5",
      "text": "Explain how @property, @classmethod and @staticmethod work via the descriptor protocol and decorate methods correctly",
      "observable": "Predict what obj.attr returns for a given descriptor and write a reusable validator descriptor"
    }
  ],
  "exclusions": [
    {
      "text": "Metaclasses and __init_subclass__",
      "why": "Alternative class-customisation tools, a separate topic beyond decorators"
    },
    {
      "text": "Static typing of decorators (ParamSpec, Concatenate)",
      "why": "Type-checker detail not needed to write or understand working decorators"
    },
    {
      "text": "Async and generator-specific decorators, contextlib.contextmanager internals",
      "why": "Builds on coroutines and generators, which this course does not teach"
    },
    {
      "text": "Framework decorators (Flask routes, pytest fixtures, dataclasses internals)",
      "why": "Library-specific APIs; the course teaches the mechanism they all share"
    },
    {
      "text": "Third-party wrapper libraries such as wrapt",
      "why": "Optional tooling; functools covers what a working learner needs"
    }
  ],
